- The pack of parts: a LIBRARY, not a page.
-
- A class reaches `web.js` and `web.view.tree` by being named here, and that is
- all the editor needs of this module: the shelf offers the two parts, the second
- level of its panel offers the primitives, and both read the tree beside the
- bundle. Nothing is drawn, so there is nothing to configure and nothing to keep
- in step with the editor.
-
- The showcase page this used to be — a title, a demo wiring and seventeen
- components with sample values in them — was scaffolding for a palette that no
- longer opens first. What it proved is proved by the tests instead.
-
- BEFORE SHORTENING THE LIST, a measurement, 09.09.2026. The bundle carries 84
- classes counting the stub, three of them ours, and 33 of the 84 exist to serve
- exactly two names below: `$mol_text` and `$mol_select`. Without those two the
- pack is 51 classes. They stay, because inside a block there is nothing else to
- lay out text and a dropdown with, and because the whole of mol is one address
- away for anyone who wants it. Cutting anything here empties the second level of
- the panel, not the showcase — the showcase is already gone.
$bog_vmap_part $mol_view
	- The parts of this pack. Everything else below is mol itself, carried along
	- so that a page can be laid out and not only assembled.
	Calc $bog_vmap_part_calc
	Map $bog_vmap_part_map
	Cell $bog_vmap_part_cell
	Plot $bog_vmap_part_plot
	-
	Button_major $mol_button_major
	Button_minor $mol_button_minor
	String $mol_string
	Textarea $mol_textarea
	Number $mol_number
	Check_box $mol_check_box
	Switch $mol_switch
	Select $mol_select
	Link $mol_link
	Image $mol_image
	Text $mol_text
	Paragraph $mol_paragraph
	Labeler $mol_labeler
	Row $mol_row
	Card $mol_card
	List $mol_list
	Form $mol_form
	Form_field $mol_form_field
